.TH CYAML_PARSE_N_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_parse_n_mp, cyaml_parse_n \- parse a bounded YAML buffer
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

cyaml cyaml_parse_n_mp(const char *yaml_str, size_t len,
                       char **err_str, ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
cyaml cyaml_parse_n(const char *yaml_str, size_t len, char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function behaves like cyaml_parse_mp(), but it reads at most len
bytes from yaml_str, and yaml_str need not be null-terminated.  This is
useful for parsing one part of a larger buffer.  The rules for a
multi-document stream are the same as those that cyaml_parse_mp()
describes.

The character rules of cyaml_parse_mp() apply to every one of the len
bytes: a null byte, any other character outside c-printable, or a
UTF-8 sequence that len cuts short is a parse error whose message gives
the line and the column.  A byte past len is never read.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
yaml_str   Input buffer, which need not be null-terminated.
len        Number of bytes to parse.
err_str    Out-parameter for the error string, or NULL to ignore it.
           It follows the rules of cyaml_parse_mp(): the library owns
           the string, and the message is printable ASCII whatever the
           len bytes hold.
mp         Custom allocator, or NULL for default.
           The library keeps its own copy of the struct, so the caller
           may release or reuse the struct once this call returns, but
           the functions that it names must stay callable until the
           last node built with them is destroyed.  A process can use
           at most 64 distinct sets of four functions; a call that
           would need a 65th fails and returns NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Root cyaml node on success, or NULL on a failure.  See cyaml_parse_mp()
for the behaviour with more than one document.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_parse_mp (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
